  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The javax.ws.rs.core classes appear to be causing issues with OSGi loading of fcrepo-camel.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When a route tries to use the FcrepoClient, a class not found error is thrown, even though the class (apparently) has been loaded into the bundle.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Since Link header parsing is the only place where the Jersey classes are being used, one option would be to parse the headers manually (split on \";\", remove leading and trailing <>, etc)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
  "duedate": null,
  "environment": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Karaf",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
