  "description": "<p>The javax.ws.rs.core classes appear to be causing issues with OSGi loading of fcrepo-camel.</p>\n\n<p>When a route tries to use the FcrepoClient, a class not found error is thrown, even though the class (apparently) has been loaded into the bundle.</p>\n\n<p>Since Link header parsing is the only place where the Jersey classes are being used, one option would be to parse the headers manually (split on \";\", remove leading and trailing &lt;&gt;, etc)</p>",
